# W3's own verification mutant. Not a slice: this is the defect that proved
# `dev prove --with` can produce a red at all, and it is kept because a tool's first red is the
# only evidence anybody has that the tool can produce one (CLAUDE.md 0.3).
#
# defect: LanePrefix requires a DOUBLE colon, so `WATER: make it darker` is no longer a tier-0
# defect: prefix at all -- the routing ladder's one instant, model-free, code-only rung.
#
# It is aimed at ONE function reached from two layers, which is what a slice's mutant has to be:
# a pure-logic test calls Daemon.LanePrefix directly, and m2 types a prefixed sentence at a real
# daemon and reads where it landed. One character reddens both.
#
# expects-red: unit:Dodona.Tests.RoutingInCodeTests.A_lane_prefix_names_its_target_and_keeps_the_rest
# expects-red: unit:Dodona.Tests.RoutingInCodeTests.A_prefixed_paragraph_keeps_its_newlines
# expects-red: m2:tier0_prefix_routes
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------ the two controls
#
# (1) THE REASON THIS MUTANT IS `::` AND NOT `return null`. The test that pins `\s+` and not
#     `\s*` -- `routekind:new-task ...` must NOT be read as a target, the bug that once created
#     a lane titled ROUTEKIND -- asserts LanePrefix returns null. A mutant that made it return
#     null ALWAYS would have reddened three checks and turned that one greener for the wrong
#     reason. A defect that satisfies the check it was not aimed at is how an over-broad mutant
#     flatters itself.
#
# expects-green: unit:Dodona.Tests.RoutingInCodeTests.A_colon_with_no_space_is_not_a_target
#
# (2) A FINDING, WRITTEN AS A CHECK RATHER THAN AS PROSE, because prose is not enforcement.
#     `m2:tier0_message_delivered` was listed expects-red on the first run of this mutant and
#     came back VACUOUS. That is correct and it is about the CHECK, not about the mutant: with
#     tier 0 dead the sentence still reached SKY, by the focus fallback -- the run printed
#     `-> SKY (focus, no classifier warm)` -- so the body still arrived and the check still
#     passed. It asserts ARRIVAL, and arrival is what the fallback also produces. Only its
#     sibling `tier0_prefix_routes` asserts the RUNG, by matching `-> SKY (tier 0)`.
#
#     This matters beyond one check: TEST-ARCHITECTURE-PLAN 2.2 names
#     `m2:tier0_message_delivered` as the owner of wire E7, whose whole sentence is "takes the
#     INSTANT path ... with no classifier consulted". Under this defect no instant path existed
#     and its owner stayed green. Recorded in tests\ledger\README.md; wires.tsv is frozen and
#     is not edited here.
#
# expects-green: m2:tier0_message_delivered
diff --git a/src/Dodona/Daemon.cs b/src/Dodona/Daemon.cs
index 54091c2..489d57d 100644
--- a/src/Dodona/Daemon.cs
+++ b/src/Dodona/Daemon.cs
@@ -5759,7 +5759,7 @@ sealed class Daemon
     internal static (string Target, string Body)? LanePrefix(string text)
     {
         var m = System.Text.RegularExpressions.Regex.Match(
-            text, @"^([A-Za-z0-9_-]+):\s+(.+)$", System.Text.RegularExpressions.RegexOptions.Singleline);
+            text, @"^([A-Za-z0-9_-]+)::\s+(.+)$", System.Text.RegularExpressions.RegexOptions.Singleline);
         return m.Success ? (m.Groups[1].Value, m.Groups[2].Value) : null;
     }
 
